    "body": "I didn't realise that this had already been bikeshedded. \r\n\r\nI would like to be pedantic and say that writableType/readableType are from the point of view of the author of the transform, whereas {writable, readable} are from the point of view of the consumer of the transform. But even I don't find this particularly convincing, so I withdraw my objection.",
